      `an originating claim in the action is about to be issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 2 the requirement to endorse the originating claim applies` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the action is an action for libel`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an originating claim in an action for libel" -- a scope limit with no "only" (ruling (c))
           IF (NOT (`an originating claim in the action is about to be issued`))
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before an originating claim in an action for libel is issued, it must be endorsed with a statement giving sufficient particulars of the publications" (the condition is not met)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

