-- Rule 3(2): "Where in an action for libel or slander the defendant alleges that (a) insofar as the words complained of consist of statements of fact, they are
-- true in substance and in fact; and (b) insofar as they consist of expressions of opinion, they are fair comment on a matter of public interest, or pleads to the
-- like effect, the defendant must give particulars ..."
