-- Rule 3(3), second limb: "but if (a) the defendant pleads that any of those words or matters are fair comment on a matter of public interest or were published upon a
-- privileged occasion; and (b) the claimant intends to allege that the defendant was actuated by express malice, the claimant must, with permission of the Court, serve a
-- reply giving particulars of the facts and matters from which the malice is to be inferred."
