-- The details required "any" or "peculiar" only where there are some: three states.
DECLARE `o 43 r 3(4) a statement may be required` IS ONE OF
    `o 43 r 3(4) it is stated`
    `o 43 r 3(4) it is not stated`
    `o 43 r 3(4) it is not applicable on these facts`

-- src:5954 | (4) Without affecting Order 6, Rule 5 and Order 9, Rule 13, the claimant must give full particulars in the statement of claim of the facts and matters on which the claimant relies in support of the claimant’s claim for damages, including details of any conduct by the defendant which it is alleged has increased the loss suffered and of any loss which is peculiar to the claimant’s own circumstances.
@ref O 43 r 3(4) (src:5954)
GIVEN statement IS A `o 43 r 3(4) a statement may be required`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 3(4) the statement is required` MEANS
    CONSIDER statement
