-- src:5954 | (4) Without affecting Order 6, Rule 5 and Order 9, Rule 13, the claimant must give full particulars in the statement of claim of the facts and matters on which the claimant relies in support of the claimant’s claim for damages, including details of any conduct by the defendant which it is alleged has increased the loss suffered and of any loss which is peculiar to the claimant’s own circumstances.
@ref O 43 r 3(4) (src:5954)
GIVEN contents IS A `o 43 r 3(4) what the statement of claim gives particulars of`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 3(4) the statement of claim gives the particulars the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF     contents's `o 43 r 3(4)(1) full particulars of the facts and matters on which the claimant relies in support of the claimant's claim for damages`
       AND (contents's `o 43 r 3(4)(2) details of any conduct by the defendant which it is alleged has increased the loss suffered` EQUALS `o 43 r 3(4) it is stated` OR contents's `o 43 r 3(4)(2) details of any conduct by the defendant which it is alleged has increased the loss suffered` EQUALS `o 43 r 3(4) it is not applicable on these facts`)
       AND (contents's `o 43 r 3(4)(3) details of any loss which is peculiar to the claimant's own circumstances` EQUALS `o 43 r 3(4) it is stated` OR contents's `o 43 r 3(4)(3) details of any loss which is peculiar to the claimant's own circumstances` EQUALS `o 43 r 3(4) it is not applicable on these facts`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); O 43 r 3(4) does not say what follows when something required is missing


