    IF `the counterclaim is a counterclaim for libel or slander`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a counterclaim for libel or slander"

-- Rule 4(1): "Where in an action for libel or slander against several defendants sued jointly the claimant, in accordance with Order 14, Rule 3(1), accepts money paid into Court by any of
-- those defendants in satisfaction of the claimant's cause of action against that defendant, then, despite anything in Rule 3(4) of Order 14, the action is stayed as against that defendant only".
-- src:5957 | 4. —(1) Where in an action for libel or slander against several defendants sued jointly the claimant, in accordance with Order 14, Rule 3(1), accepts money paid into Court by any of those defendants in satisfaction of the claimant’s cause of action against that defendant, then, despite anything in Rule 3(4) of Order 14, the action is stayed as against that defendant only, but — ( a )
@ref O 43 r 4(1) (src:5957)
GIVEN `the action is an action for libel or slander against several defendants sued jointly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant, in accordance with Order 14, Rule 3(1), accepts money paid into Court by one of those defendants in satisfaction of the claimant's cause of action against that defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant in question is the defendant who paid the money into Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 4(1) the action is stayed as against the defendant` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`the action is an action for libel or slander against several defendants sued jointly` AND `the claimant, in accordance with Order 14, Rule 3(1), accepts money paid into Court by one of those defendants in satisfaction of the claimant's cause of action against that defendant`))
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in an action for libel or slander against several defendants sued jointly the claimant, in accordance with Order 14, Rule 3(1), accepts money paid into Court by any of those defendants" (the condition is not met)
           IF `the defendant in question is the defendant who paid the money into Court`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the action is stayed as against that defendant only"

-- (a): "the sum recoverable under any judgment given in the claimant's favour against any other defendant in the action by way of damages must not exceed the amount (if any) by which the
-- amount of the damages exceeds the amount paid into Court by the defendant as against whom the action has been stayed".  A number, so a yes/no twin says whether the cap applies.
-- src:5957 | 4. —(1) Where in an action for libel or slander against several defendants sued jointly the claimant, in accordance with Order 14, Rule 3(1), accepts money paid into Court by any of those defendants in satisfaction of the claimant’s cause of action against that defendant, then, despite anything in Rule 3(4) of Order 14, the action is stayed as against that defendant only, but — ( a )
-- src:5958 | the sum recoverable under any judgment given in the claimant’s favour against any other defendant in the action by way of damages must not exceed the amount (if any) by which the amount of the damages exceeds the amount paid into Court by the defendant as against whom the action has been stayed; and
@ref O 43 r 4(1) (src:5957-5958)
GIVEN `the action has been stayed under paragraph (1) as against one defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum is recoverable against another defendant by way of damages` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 4(1)(a) the cap on the sum recoverable from another defendant applies` MEANS
    IF `the action has been stayed under paragraph (1) as against one defendant` AND `the sum is recoverable against another defendant by way of damages`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the sum recoverable under any judgment given in the claimant's favour against any other defendant in the action by way of damages" (the stay under paragraph (1) has not arisen, or the sum is not damages against another defendant)

-- src:5958 | the sum recoverable under any judgment given in the claimant’s favour against any other defendant in the action by way of damages must not exceed the amount (if any) by which the amount of the damages exceeds the amount paid into Court by the defendant as against whom the action has been stayed; and
@ref O 43 r 4(1) (src:5958)
GIVEN `the action has been stayed under paragraph (1) as against one defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the damages` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid into Court by the defendant as against whom the action has been stayed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 43 r 4(1)(a) the most that is recoverable from another defendant by way of damages` MEANS
    IF `the action has been stayed under paragraph (1) as against one defendant`
    THEN JUST (IF `the amount of the damages` AT MOST `the amount paid into Court by the defendant as against whom the action has been stayed` THEN 0 ELSE `the amount of the damages` - `the amount paid into Court by the defendant as against whom the action has been stayed`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the cap is asked only where the stay under paragraph (1) has arisen; `o 43 r 4(1)(a) the cap on the sum recoverable from another defendant applies` answers JUST FALSE

-- (b): "the claimant is not entitled to the claimant's costs of the action against the other defendant after the date of the payment into Court unless either the amount of the damages
-- awarded to the claimant is greater than the amount paid into Court and accepted by the claimant or the Judge is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for the claimant to
-- proceed with the action against the other defendant."  A bar with "unless" (QA).
-- FORK QA | the "unless" is met (damages awarded greater than the amount paid in, or the Judge's opinion): NOTHING (a lifted bar grants nothing) | JUST TRUE (the exception permits it)
-- src:5959 | ( b )
-- src:5960 | the claimant is not entitled to the claimant’s costs of the action against the other defendant after the date of the payment into Court unless either the amount of the damages awarded to the claimant is greater than the amount paid into Court and accepted by the claimant or the Judge is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for the claimant to proceed with the action against the other defendant.
@ref O 43 r 4(1) (src:5959-5960)
GIVEN `the action has been stayed under paragraph (1) as against one defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are the claimant's costs of the action against the other defendant after the date of the payment into Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the damages awarded to the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid into Court and accepted by the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the Judge is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for the claimant to proceed with the action against the other defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 4(1)(b) the claimant is entitled to the claimant's costs against the other defendant after the payment into Court` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the action has been stayed under paragraph (1) as against one defendant`) OR (NOT `the costs are the claimant's costs of the action against the other defendant after the date of the payment into Court`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the claimant's costs of the action against the other defendant after the date of the payment into Court"
           IF `the amount of the damages awarded to the claimant` GREATER THAN `the amount paid into Court and accepted by the claimant`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless either the amount of the damages awarded to the claimant is greater than the amount paid into Court and accepted" -- the bar is lifted and grants nothing (QA)
           IF `the Judge is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for the claimant to proceed with the action against the other defendant`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "or the Judge is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground" -- the bar is lifted and grants nothing (QA)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claimant is not entitled to the claimant's costs of the action against the other defendant after the date of the payment into Court"

-- The same paragraph as the question a party asks, "is the claimant barred from those costs?": JUST TRUE while the bar bites, JUST FALSE once either "unless" limb is met.
-- src:5959 | ( b )
-- src:5960 | the claimant is not entitled to the claimant’s costs of the action against the other defendant after the date of the payment into Court unless either the amount of the damages awarded to the claimant is greater than the amount paid into Court and accepted by the claimant or the Judge is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for the claimant to proceed with the action against the other defendant.
@ref O 43 r 4(1) (src:5959-5960)
GIVEN `the action has been stayed under paragraph (1) as against one defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are the claimant's costs of the action against the other defendant after the date of the payment into Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the damages awarded to the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid into Court and accepted by the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the Judge is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for the claimant to proceed with the action against the other defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 4(1)(b) the bar on the claimant's costs against the other defendant applies` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the action has been stayed under paragraph (1) as against one defendant`) OR (NOT `the costs are the claimant's costs of the action against the other defendant after the date of the payment into Court`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the claimant's costs of the action against the other defendant after the date of the payment into Court"
           IF `the amount of the damages awarded to the claimant` GREATER THAN `the amount paid into Court and accepted by the claimant`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless either the amount of the damages awarded to the claimant is greater than the amount paid into Court and accepted" -- the bar ends
           IF `the Judge is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for the claimant to proceed with the action against the other defendant`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or the Judge is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground" -- the bar ends
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Rule 4(2): "Where in an action for libel a party pleads the defence for which section 10(2) of the Defamation Act provides, Order 14, Rule 7 does not apply in relation to that pleading."
-- MARGINAL b | the function asks whether Order 14, Rule 7 applies: JUST FALSE inside the "where" (the text's own flat negative), NOTHING outside it (the Rule says nothing there) | JUST FALSE outside the "where" (periods ruling (b))
-- src:5961 | (2) Where in an action for libel a party pleads the defence for which section 10(2) of the Defamation Act provides, Order 14, Rule 7 does not apply in relation to that pleading.
@ref O 43 r 4(2) (src:5961)
GIVEN `the action is an action for libel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party pleads the defence for which section 10(2) of the Defamation Act provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 4(2) Order 14, Rule 7 applies to the pleading` MEANS
    IF `the action is an action for libel` AND `a party pleads the defence for which section 10(2) of the Defamation Act provides`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Order 14, Rule 7 does not apply in relation to that pleading"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where in an action for libel a party pleads the defence for which section 10(2) of the Defamation Act provides"

-- Rule 5(1): "Where a party accepts money paid into Court in satisfaction of a cause of action for libel or slander, the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) may apply to a Judge in Chambers by
-- summons for permission to make in open court a statement in terms approved by the Judge."
-- src:5963 | 5. —(1) Where a party accepts money paid into Court in satisfaction of a cause of action for libel or slander, the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) may apply to a Judge in Chambers by summons for permission to make in open court a statement in terms approved by the Judge. (2) Where a party to an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial desires to make a statement in open court, an application must be made to the Court for an order that the action be set down for trial, and before the date fixed for the trial the statement must be submitted for the approval of the Judge before whom it is to be made.
@ref O 43 r 5(1) (src:5963)
GIVEN `a party accepts money paid into Court in satisfaction of a cause of action for libel or slander` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is the claimant or the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to a Judge in Chambers by summons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 5(1) the party may apply for permission to make a statement in open court` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `a party accepts money paid into Court in satisfaction of a cause of action for libel or slander`)
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a party accepts money paid into Court in satisfaction of a cause of action for libel or slander"
           IF `the applicant is the claimant or the defendant` AND `the application is made to a Judge in Chambers by summons`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) may apply to a Judge in Chambers by summons"

-- Rule 5(2): "Where a party to an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial desires to make a statement in open court, an application must be made to the Court for an order
-- that the action be set down for trial, and before the date fixed for the trial the statement must be submitted for the approval of the Judge before whom it is to be made."
-- src:5963 | 5. —(1) Where a party accepts money paid into Court in satisfaction of a cause of action for libel or slander, the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) may apply to a Judge in Chambers by summons for permission to make in open court a statement in terms approved by the Judge. (2) Where a party to an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial desires to make a statement in open court, an application must be made to the Court for an order that the action be set down for trial, and before the date fixed for the trial the statement must be submitted for the approval of the Judge before whom it is to be made.
@ref O 43 r 5(2) (src:5963)
GIVEN `the action is an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party desires to make a statement in open court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 5(2) the party's duty to apply and to submit the statement arises` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`the action is an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial` AND `a party desires to make a statement in open court`))
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a party to an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial desires to make a statement in open court, an application must be made to the Court for an order that the action be set down for trial, and before the date fixed for the trial the statement must be submitted for the approval of the Judge" (the condition is not met)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- FORK QB | bare "must" (Where a party to an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial desires to make a statement in open court, an application must be made to the Court for an order that the action be set down for trial, and before the date fixed for the trial the statement must be submitted for the approval of the Judge): the requirement is not met | NOTHING | JUST FALSE for the compliance question
-- FORK QD | the duty does not arise (the "where", "before" or "unless" is unmet): NOTHING, with the companion `o 43 r 5(2) the party's duty to apply and to submit the statement arises` answering JUST FALSE | JUST TRUE ("nothing is unmet")
-- src:5963 | 5. —(1) Where a party accepts money paid into Court in satisfaction of a cause of action for libel or slander, the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) may apply to a Judge in Chambers by summons for permission to make in open court a statement in terms approved by the Judge. (2) Where a party to an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial desires to make a statement in open court, an application must be made to the Court for an order that the action be set down for trial, and before the date fixed for the trial the statement must be submitted for the approval of the Judge before whom it is to be made.
@ref O 43 r 5(2) (src:5963)
GIVEN `the action is an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party desires to make a statement in open court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application has been made to the Court for an order that the action be set down for trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement has been submitted for the approval of the Judge before whom it is to be made before the date fixed for the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 5(2) the party has applied and submitted the statement as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`the action is an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial` AND `a party desires to make a statement in open court`))
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a party to an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial desires to make a statement in open court, an application must be made to the Court for an order that the action be set down for trial, and before the date fixed for the trial the statement must be submitted for the approval of the Judge" -- the duty does not arise (QD); `o 43 r 5(2) the party's duty to apply and to submit the statement arises` answers JUST FALSE
           IF `an application has been made to the Court for an order that the action be set down for trial` AND `the statement has been submitted for the approval of the Judge before whom it is to be made before the date fixed for the trial`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); O 43 r 5(2) does not say what follows when a requirement is not met

-- MARGINAL a | the statement is submitted before the date fixed for the trial: the window the text states in its own words (periods ruling (a)); done outside it is JUST FALSE, and the compliance question stays NOTHING (a bare "must", QB) | NOTHING outside the window
-- src:5963 | 5. —(1) Where a party accepts money paid into Court in satisfaction of a cause of action for libel or slander, the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) may apply to a Judge in Chambers by summons for permission to make in open court a statement in terms approved by the Judge. (2) Where a party to an action for libel or slander which is settled before the trial desires to make a statement in open court, an application must be made to the Court for an order that the action be set down for trial, and before the date fixed for the trial the statement must be submitted for the approval of the Judge before whom it is to be made.
@ref O 43 r 5(2) (src:5963)
GIVEN `the statement has been submitted for the approval of the Judge before whom it is to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement was submitted before the date fixed for the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 5(2) the statement is submitted before the date fixed for the trial` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the statement has been submitted for the approval of the Judge before whom it is to be made`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): it has not been done, so there is nothing to place in or outside the window; O 43 r 5(2) does not say what follows (QB)
           IF (NOT `the statement was submitted before the date fixed for the trial`)
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the date fixed for the trial the statement must be submitted for the approval of the Judge before whom it is to be made"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


-- Rule 6: "In an action for libel and slander in which the defendant does not by the defendant's defence assert the truth of the statement complained of, the defendant is not entitled at the
-- trial or hearing to give evidence-in-chief, with a view to mitigation of damages, as to the circumstances under which the libel or slander was published, or as to the character of the
-- claimant, without the permission of the Court, unless (a) such matters are included in the defendant's defence filed and served in the action; or (b) where no defence has been filed and
-- served, directions have been obtained from the Registrar pursuant to Order 15, Rule 15(4) for the inclusion of such evidence."
-- FORK QA | the permission of the Court or an exception (a) or (b) is met: NOTHING (a lifted bar grants nothing) | JUST TRUE (the exception permits it)
-- MARGINAL b | the bar is stated for "an action for libel and slander in which the defendant does not ... assert the truth": outside that action the function answers NOTHING (a scope limit) | JUST FALSE (periods ruling (b), "in which" read as "where")
-- src:5965 | 6. In an action for libel and slander in which the defendant does not by the defendant’s defence assert the truth of the statement complained of, the defendant is not entitled at the trial or hearing to give evidence ‑ in ‑ chief, with a view to mitigation of damages, as to the circumstances under which the libel or slander was published, or as to the character of the claimant, without the permission of the Court, unless — ( a )
-- src:5966 | such matters are included in the defendant’s defence filed and served in the action; or
-- src:5967 | ( b )
-- src:5968 | where no defence has been filed and served, directions have been obtained from the Registrar pursuant to Order 15, Rule 15(4) for the inclusion of such evidence.
@ref O 43 r 6 (src:5965-5968)
GIVEN `the action is an action for libel or slander in which the defendant does not by the defence assert the truth of the statement complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is evidence-in-chief with a view to mitigation of damages as to the circumstances under which the libel or slander was published, or as to the character of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a defence has been filed and served in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `such matters are included in the defendant's defence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `directions have been obtained from the Registrar pursuant to Order 15, Rule 15(4) for the inclusion of such evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 6 the defendant is entitled to give the evidence at the trial or hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the action is an action for libel or slander in which the defendant does not by the defence assert the truth of the statement complained of`) OR (NOT `the evidence is evidence-in-chief with a view to mitigation of damages as to the circumstances under which the libel or slander was published, or as to the character of the claimant`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In an action for libel and slander in which the defendant does not by the defendant's defence assert the truth of the statement complained of ... evidence-in-chief, with a view to mitigation of damages"
           IF `the Court has given permission`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the permission of the Court" -- the bar is lifted and grants nothing (QA)
           IF `a defence has been filed and served in the action` AND `such matters are included in the defendant's defence`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless (a) such matters are included in the defendant's defence filed and served in the action" -- the bar is lifted and grants nothing (QA)
           IF (NOT `a defence has been filed and served in the action`) AND `directions have been obtained from the Registrar pursuant to Order 15, Rule 15(4) for the inclusion of such evidence`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "or (b) where no defence has been filed and served, directions have been obtained from the Registrar" -- the bar is lifted and grants nothing (QA)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the defendant is not entitled at the trial or hearing to give evidence-in-chief, with a view to mitigation of damages, ... without the permission of the Court"

-- The same paragraph as the question a party asks, "is the defendant barred from that evidence?": JUST TRUE while the bar bites, JUST FALSE once the permission is given or exception (a) or (b) is met.
-- src:5965 | 6. In an action for libel and slander in which the defendant does not by the defendant’s defence assert the truth of the statement complained of, the defendant is not entitled at the trial or hearing to give evidence ‑ in ‑ chief, with a view to mitigation of damages, as to the circumstances under which the libel or slander was published, or as to the character of the claimant, without the permission of the Court, unless — ( a )
-- src:5966 | such matters are included in the defendant’s defence filed and served in the action; or
-- src:5967 | ( b )
-- src:5968 | where no defence has been filed and served, directions have been obtained from the Registrar pursuant to Order 15, Rule 15(4) for the inclusion of such evidence.
@ref O 43 r 6 (src:5965-5968)
GIVEN `the action is an action for libel or slander in which the defendant does not by the defence assert the truth of the statement complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is evidence-in-chief with a view to mitigation of damages as to the circumstances under which the libel or slander was published, or as to the character of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a defence has been filed and served in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `such matters are included in the defendant's defence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `directions have been obtained from the Registrar pursuant to Order 15, Rule 15(4) for the inclusion of such evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 6 the bar on the defendant's evidence applies` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the action is an action for libel or slander in which the defendant does not by the defence assert the truth of the statement complained of`) OR (NOT `the evidence is evidence-in-chief with a view to mitigation of damages as to the circumstances under which the libel or slander was published, or as to the character of the claimant`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In an action for libel and slander in which the defendant does not by the defendant's defence assert the truth of the statement complained of ... evidence-in-chief, with a view to mitigation of damages"
           IF `the Court has given permission`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the permission of the Court" -- with the permission the bar ends
           IF `a defence has been filed and served in the action` AND `such matters are included in the defendant's defence`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless (a) such matters are included in the defendant's defence filed and served in the action" -- the bar ends
           IF (NOT `a defence has been filed and served in the action`) AND `directions have been obtained from the Registrar pursuant to Order 15, Rule 15(4) for the inclusion of such evidence`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or (b) where no defence has been filed and served, directions have been obtained from the Registrar" -- the bar ends
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Rule 7: "An application to the Court under section 7 of the Defamation Act to determine any question as to the steps to be taken in fulfilment of an offer of amends made under that section may
-- only be heard by a Judge in person."
-- src:5970 | 7. An application to the Court under section 7 of the Defamation Act to determine any question as to the steps to be taken in fulfilment of an offer of amends made under that section may only be heard by a Judge in person.
@ref O 43 r 7 (src:5970)
GIVEN `the application is an application under section 7 of the Defamation Act to determine a question as to the steps to be taken in fulfilment of an offer of amends made under that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who hears it` IS A `Decision maker`
      `the Judge hears it in person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 43 r 7 the application may be heard by the person` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the application is an application under section 7 of the Defamation Act to determine a question as to the steps to be taken in fulfilment of an offer of amends made under that section`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application to the Court under section 7 of the Defamation Act to determine any question as to the steps to be taken in fulfilment of an offer of amends"
           IF `who hears it` EQUALS `A Judge` AND `the Judge hears it in person`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be heard by a Judge in person"
